+# repository, with D3DDevice_GetRenderTarget2 0x1D5170 and GetDepthStencilSurface2 0x1D5190 signed although that
+# game leaves them to the library). Names that title does not link stay {} (no signature).
+
+# XDK library signatures read by xbe_symbols, written by xbe_symbols in sign mode. No library bytes stored.
+# [symbols] name = {sec, len, hash, calls, deep, count, nth}: hash of len bytes from the function start in
+# section sec, image addresses and rel32 targets masked; calls = [len, hash, calls] of each rel32 call or
+# jump target outside it, in order, two levels deep; deep = lookalikes exist, so the callees' callees must
+# match too; count and nth pick one of identical functions by link order; xtlid = its .XTLID export id,
+# used when the bytes match nothing. {} = no signature, stays 0.
+# k = its constants, sorted: immediates and displacements of instructions that do not use the stack, when
+# not an image address, a branch target or below 0x40; an address inside .text counts in a library section,
+# which holds no such pointer. ret = stack bytes its rets pop, regs = registers it reads before it writes
+# them. A function the bytes do not find is matched by k; ret and regs then show a changed convention.
+# [anchors] functions only used to find data. [data] in = function, insn = instruction index, op = operand,
+# deref = offsets of the dwords then read in turn, for data behind a table, xtlid = the id .XTLID lists the
+# address under, used when in finds nothing.
